# Findings in git history that gitleaks is right to flag and that are not
# actionable, one line each, with the reason.
#
# Only a fingerprint that has been looked at belongs here. Blanket-allowlisting
# a path is what would make this gate worthless: testdata/fixtures/ is recorded
# from the live API, so it is exactly where a real credential would hide, and it
# is not excluded as a directory.
#
# A fingerprint contains the commit it was found in, so rewriting history
# invalidates every line of this file. If the entries here stop matching, that is
# why, and the fix is to re-run gitleaks and record the new ones rather than to
# widen the rules.
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There used to be a fourth entry here, for a real access token committed by a
# test written to prove that tokens do not leak. It is gone rather than
# allowlisted: the history was rewritten on 2026-07-31 to replace the value.
# An ignore file that points at a commit containing a credential is a map, not a
# mitigation, and that argument got sharper when the repository became public.
# What happened is recorded in the git history of this file and in the pull
# request, which is where it belongs.
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. A hand-written fixture value that says REDACTED in it.
#
# testdata/fixtures/file/info.json carries a TempStreamingLink whose temp_auth
# parameter is the marker file_test.go asserts gets redacted (§9.4). The file id
# is base64 "ExampleFileID", the owner is "Tester Tester" and the hash is the MD5
# of an empty string: the whole fixture is constructed, not recorded. Flagged for
# entropy in a value that literally contains the word REDACTED.
30d6a0d10e0b4524c8dccd243d1551c17722d8c2:testdata/fixtures/file/info.json:generic-api-key:17

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. A password this test puts on a file it created and then deletes.
#
# TestSandboxPasswordDoesNotGateTheOwner sets a password on a throwaway file to
# prove D32: the password gates the public web page only, and the owner is never
# asked for it. It is not a credential for anything — no account, no session, no
# file that outlives the test. The working tree now uses an obviously synthetic
# value; this entry covers the commit where it did not.
2de0a74a272da655fa3039f08b0a2e41195895ad:pkg/opendrive/download_integration_test.go:generic-api-key:320

